# {{SITE_NAME}} — project rules

The website for {{SITE_NAME}}, live at <https://{{SITE_DOMAIN}}>. {{STACK_NOTE}}
The site lives in `web/`. Deployed to Cloudflare Pages (project `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`).

This repo is the only source of truth for the site's content.

## Workflow — never push to main

Always create a branch and open a pull request. CI builds every pull request and posts a
preview URL as a comment; merging to `main` deploys production.

Do not run `wrangler pages deploy` by hand — CI owns deployment. Deploying manually puts
the live site out of step with this repo, which is the exact confusion the preview
workflow exists to prevent.

Before opening a pull request, run `npm run build` inside `web/` and confirm it succeeds
with no errors. A build that fails in CI wastes the reviewer's time and blocks the
preview link they are waiting for.

