## Where content lives (edit data, not markup, when possible)

{{CONTENT_MAP}}

Text belongs in the data files, not in the markup. It is what makes a future request
like "change that sentence" a reliable lookup rather than a search that can miss a copy.

## Contact form

Sends through Brevo from a Cloudflare Pages Function at `web/functions/api/contact.js`.

Bindings on the Pages project: `BREVO_API_KEY` (secret, required), `CONTACT_TO`,
`CONTACT_FROM` (optional).

The key is bound to the **production environment only**, so preview deployments cannot
send mail. That is deliberate. Don't read it as a broken build.

Pages binds environment variables at deploy time — after adding or rotating a secret,
redeploy or the running site will not see it.

The form must keep working without JavaScript. The no-JS path is a plain form post
answered with a redirect carrying `?sent=1|0`; the enhanced path is a `fetch` that gets
JSON back. Both are load-bearing — the plain path is the fallback when anything else
fails.

